/-!
# The bipolar rate under weak lower semicontinuity, and for weakly compact nulls

The bipolar rate `bipolarRate Q S` of a probability measure `Q` against an i.i.d. null `S` of
probability measures is at most the smallest relative entropy `klInf Q S`. LMLExplore proves that
they are equal when `R ↦ klInf R S` is lower semicontinuous at `Q` for the topology generated by
the integrals of the bounded measurable functions
(`ProbabilityTheory.bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_forall_exists_forall_le`). This file derives the form
of [RR26, Theorem 4.1], for the topology of weak convergence of probability measures
(`MeasureTheory.ProbabilityMeasure`), and its case of a weakly compact null.

* On any topological space whose σ-algebra contains the open sets, lower semicontinuity of
  `R ↦ klInf R S` at `Q` for the weak topology gives `bipolarRate Q S = klInf Q S`: every weak
  neighbourhood of `Q` contains the probability measures whose integrals of some finitely many
  bounded continuous functions are within some `ε > 0` of those of `Q`, and bounded continuous
  functions are bounded and measurable.
* [RR26] states the lower semicontinuity with sequences,
  `klInf Q S ≤ liminf (klInf (R k) S)` whenever `R k` converges weakly to `Q`, that is, Tau Ceti's
  `TauCeti.SeqLowerSemicontinuousAt`. It suffices where the weak neighbourhoods of `Q` are
  countably generated, which holds on every separable pseudo-metrizable space, where the weak
  topology is pseudo-metrizable by the Lévy–Prokhorov metric, in particular on a Polish space.
  The file imports `Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.LevyProkhorovMetric`, whose instance provides
  that hypothesis there.
* On a pseudo-metrizable space with its Borel σ-algebra, if the members of the null form a compact
  set of `ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧`, then `R ↦ klInf R S` is lower semicontinuous: it is the infimum
  over a compact set of the relative entropy, which is jointly lower semicontinuous for the weak
  topology (Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.lowerSemicontinuous_klDiv_probabilityMeasure`). Hence
  `bipolarRate Q S = klInf Q S` for every probability measure `Q`.

[RR26, Theorem 4.1] assumes a Polish space, a nonempty null and `klInf Q S < ∞`. None of these is
assumed here: the first statement holds on every topological space whose σ-algebra contains the
open sets, the compact case on every pseudo-metrizable space with its Borel σ-algebra, the null
may be empty and the common value infinite.

## Main statements

* `ProbabilityTheory.bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_lowerSemicontinuousAt`: the bipolar rate equals the
  smallest relative entropy under lower semicontinuity at `Q` for the weak topology.
* `ProbabilityTheory.bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_seqLowerSemicontinuousAt`: the same under the
  sequential lower semicontinuity of [RR26], where the weak neighbourhoods of `Q` are countably
  generated.
* `ProbabilityTheory.lowerSemicontinuous_klInf_of_isCompact`: for a weakly compact null,
  `R ↦ klInf R S` is lower semicontinuous for the weak topology.
* `ProbabilityTheory.bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_isCompact`: for a weakly compact null, the bipolar
  rate equals the smallest relative entropy at every probability measure.

## Implementation notes

The statements and proofs are adapted from `EValuesResearch/Results/WeakSemicontinuity.lean`
(commit `83205cb`) in the paper project `RemyDegenne/evalues_research`, rewritten on the API of
LMLExplore. The neighbourhood form is proved by contradiction: if every finite set `F` of bounded
continuous functions and every tolerance `1 / (n + 1)` admitted a probability measure close to `Q`
on `F` at relative entropy below `c` from the null, these measures, indexed by the pairs `(F, n)`,
would converge weakly to `Q`, against the lower semicontinuity at `Q`.

## References

* [RR26] A. Ram and A. Ramdas, *The optimal betting wealth growth rate*, arXiv:2604.25280v1.
* [EVR26] *Answers to open questions in e-values and anytime-valid inference*, notes 01 to 34 and
  the Lean library `EValuesResearch` of github.com/RemyDegenne/evalues_research, 2026; written and
  refereed by AI agents.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory InformationTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal Topology BoundedContinuousFunction

namespace ProbabilityTheory

variable {𝓧 : Type*} [TopologicalSpace 𝓧] {m𝓧 : MeasurableSpace 𝓧}

/-- **The bipolar rate under weak lower semicontinuity** [RR26, Theorem 4.1]. If the smallest
relative entropy to a null `S` of probability measures, as a function of
`R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧`, is lower semicontinuous at `Q` for the topology of weak convergence,
then the bipolar rate of `Q` against `S` equals the smallest relative entropy from `Q` to `S`. The
space is any topological space whose σ-algebra contains the open sets; the null may be empty and
the common value infinite. -/
theorem bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_lowerSemicontinuousAt [OpensMeasurableSpace 𝓧]
    (Q : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧) (S : Set (Measure 𝓧)) (hS : ∀ P ∈ S, IsProbabilityMeasure P)
    (h : LowerSemicontinuousAt (fun R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 ↦ klInf (R : Measure 𝓧) S) Q) :
    bipolarRate (Q : Measure 𝓧) S = klInf (Q : Measure 𝓧) S := by
  classical
  refine bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_forall_exists_forall_le (Q : Measure 𝓧) S hS fun c hc ↦ ?_
  by_contra! hcon
  -- every finite set `F` of bounded continuous functions and every tolerance `1 / (n + 1)` admit
  -- a probability measure close to `Q` on `F` at relative entropy below `c` from the null
  have key (F : Finset (𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ)) (n : ℕ) : ∃ R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧,
      (∀ g ∈ F, |∫ x, g x ∂(R : Measure 𝓧) - ∫ x, g x ∂(Q : Measure 𝓧)| ≤ 1 / (n + 1)) ∧
        klInf (R : Measure 𝓧) S < c := by
    obtain ⟨R, hR, hclose, hlt⟩ := hcon F.card (fun i ↦ F.equivFin.symm i) (1 / (n + 1))
      Nat.one_div_pos_of_nat (fun i ↦ (F.equivFin.symm i : 𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ).continuous.measurable)
      fun i ↦ ⟨‖(F.equivFin.symm i : 𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ)‖, fun x ↦ by
        simpa only [Real.norm_eq_abs] using (F.equivFin.symm i : 𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ).norm_coe_le_norm x⟩
    exact ⟨⟨R, hR⟩, fun g hg ↦ by simpa using hclose (F.equivFin ⟨g, hg⟩), hlt⟩
  choose R hRclose hRlt using key
  -- along the pairs `(F, n)`, these measures converge weakly to `Q`
  have htend : Tendsto (fun p : Finset (𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ) × ℕ ↦ R p.1 p.2) atTop (𝓝 Q) := by
    refine ProbabilityMeasure.tendsto_iff_forall_integral_tendsto.2 fun g ↦
      Metric.tendsto_nhds.2 fun ε hε ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_nat_one_div_lt hε
    filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop (({g}, N) : Finset (𝓧 →ᵇ ℝ) × ℕ)] with p hp
    refine (hRclose p.1 p.2 g (Finset.singleton_subset_iff.1 hp.1)).trans_lt (lt_of_le_of_lt ?_ hN)
    gcongr
    exact_mod_cast hp.2
  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := (htend.eventually (h c hc)).exists
  exact lt_asymm hp (hRlt p.1 p.2)

/-- **The bipolar rate under sequential weak lower semicontinuity** [RR26, Theorem 4.1]. If
`klInf Q S ≤ liminf (klInf (R k) S)` for every sequence of probability measures `R k` that
converges weakly to `Q` (Tau Ceti's `TauCeti.SeqLowerSemicontinuousAt`, see
`TauCeti.seqLowerSemicontinuousAt_iff_le_liminf`), the hypothesis of [RR26], then the bipolar rate
of `Q` against `S` equals the smallest relative entropy from `Q` to `S`. The weak neighbourhoods of
`Q` are assumed countably generated, which Mathlib's Lévy–Prokhorov instance provides on every
separable pseudo-metrizable space, in particular on a Polish space. -/
theorem bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_seqLowerSemicontinuousAt [OpensMeasurableSpace 𝓧]
    (Q : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧) [(𝓝 Q).IsCountablyGenerated] (S : Set (Measure 𝓧))
    (hS : ∀ P ∈ S, IsProbabilityMeasure P)
    (h : TauCeti.SeqLowerSemicontinuousAt
      (fun R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 ↦ klInf (R : Measure 𝓧) S) Q) :
    bipolarRate (Q : Measure 𝓧) S = klInf (Q : Measure 𝓧) S :=
  bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_lowerSemicontinuousAt Q S hS h.lowerSemicontinuousAt

/-- **The smallest relative entropy to a weakly compact null is weakly lower semicontinuous.** On
a pseudo-metrizable space with its Borel σ-algebra, if the members of a null `S` of probability
measures form a compact set of `ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧`, then `R ↦ klInf R S` is lower
semicontinuous for the topology of weak convergence [RR26, Section 2]. It is the infimum over a
compact set of the jointly lower semicontinuous relative entropy. -/
theorem lowerSemicontinuous_klInf_of_isCompact [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace 𝓧]
    [BorelSpace 𝓧] (S : Set (Measure 𝓧)) (hS : ∀ P ∈ S, IsProbabilityMeasure P)
    (hS_compact : IsCompact {P : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 | (P : Measure 𝓧) ∈ S}) :
    LowerSemicontinuous fun R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 ↦ klInf (R : Measure 𝓧) S := by
  set K := {P : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 | (P : Measure 𝓧) ∈ S}
  have hSK : (↑) '' K = S := image_preimage_eq_of_subset fun P hP ↦ ⟨⟨P, hS P hP⟩, rfl⟩
  have heq (R : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧) : klInf (R : Measure 𝓧) S =
      ((⨅ P ∈ K, klDiv (R : Measure 𝓧) (P : Measure 𝓧) : ℝ≥0∞) : EReal) := by
    rw [klInf_eq_coe_iInf_klDiv fun P hP ↦ by simp [(hS P hP).measure_univ],
      ← iInf_image (f := ((↑) : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 → Measure 𝓧)) (g := klDiv (R : Measure 𝓧)),
      hSK]
  simp_rw [heq]
  exact continuous_coe_ennreal_ereal.comp_lowerSemicontinuous
    (fun R ↦ UpperHemicontinuousAt.const.lowerSemicontinuousAt_biInf hS_compact fun P _ ↦
      TauCeti.lowerSemicontinuous_klDiv_probabilityMeasure (R, P))
    fun _ _ ↦ EReal.coe_ennreal_le_coe_ennreal_iff.2

/-- **The bipolar rate against a weakly compact null** [RR26, Theorem 4.1]. On a pseudo-metrizable
space with its Borel σ-algebra, if the members of a null `S` of probability measures form a compact
set of `ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧`, then for every probability measure `Q` the bipolar rate of `Q`
against `S` equals the smallest relative entropy from `Q` to `S`. -/
theorem bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_isCompact [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace 𝓧]
    [BorelSpace 𝓧] (Q : Measure 𝓧) [IsProbabilityMeasure Q] (S : Set (Measure 𝓧))
    (hS : ∀ P ∈ S, IsProbabilityMeasure P)
    (hS_compact : IsCompact {P : ProbabilityMeasure 𝓧 | (P : Measure 𝓧) ∈ S}) :
    bipolarRate Q S = klInf Q S :=
  bipolarRate_eq_klInf_of_lowerSemicontinuousAt ⟨Q, ‹_›⟩ S hS
    (lowerSemicontinuous_klInf_of_isCompact S hS hS_compact _)

end ProbabilityTheory
